  "progression": "The adopted 2026–2027 Dutch-route regulations, annual plan pp. 22–23, determine the 60 EC per year ledger and neutral choice order. The study guide lists Maghreb before Latin America in its second-period menu. Both are eligible, and this illustration follows the adopted annual plan order consistently. Year three starts with 30 EC of profiling space, then requires Culture, Religion and Knowledge and one global research seminar, colloquium and thesis. Regulations arts. 9.1 and 12.1–12.2 control progression and elective rules. The Dutch test is 0 EC. The current late-medieval and early-modern seminar uses Low Countries manuscripts and early print for lay devotion. The chosen global seminar uses photography in modern politics. Topics can change.",
  "routeSelection": {
    "route": "General direction",
    "selectionRule": "least-specialized-general",
    "basis": "Broadest Dutch-taught route. Illustrative electives and the extra research seminar follow the order in the adopted annual plan."
  },
